.TH FREAD 3S
.SH NAME
fread, fwrite \- buffered binary input/output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <stdio.h>"
.sp
.B "fread(ptr, sizeof(*ptr), nitems, stream)"
.B "FILE *stream;"
.sp
.B "fwrite(ptr, sizeof(*ptr), nitems, stream)"
.B "FILE *stream;"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fread
reads, into a block beginning at
.IR ptr ,
.I nitems
of data of the type of
.I *ptr
from the named input
.IR stream .
It returns the number of items actually
read.
.PP
.B fwrite
appends at most
.I nitems
of data of the type of
.I *ptr
beginning at
.I ptr
to the named output
.IR stream .
It returns the number of items actually
written.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
read(2), write(2), fopen(3), getc(3), putc(3), gets(3), puts(3), printf(3),
scanf(3)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B fread
and
.B fwrite
return 0 upon end of file or error.
.sp
